            <ArticleTitle>[Double blind study of tiapride in neoplasia-related pains (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2020-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The antalgic effects of tiapride used by intravenous way have been evaluated in a randomized study on 30 patients with neoplasia-related pains. We noticed a partial or a complete positive response in 60 % of the cases when tiapride is given at a dose of 300 mg/day. The average efficient period was about four hours. Tolerance was good.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
